        "node_id": "n_4_877024",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous solution was due to an incorrect initialization of the DP table. The base case should be set to 0 for all speeds except the initial speed v1, not just v1 itself. This oversight led to incorrect calculations in the dynamic programming approach. The correct initialization should be dp[0][v1] = 0 and dp[0][j] = -inf for all j ≠ v1. This ensures that the car starts at the correct speed and prevents invalid speed transitions in the first second.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5568593316456567681",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_877024_0",
